    },
    {
      "id": "when-to-use",
      "title": "When to use it",
      "body": "Use it after Xin chào, Chào bạn, a first introduction, a class, a tour meetup, or a friendly repeated interaction. It is less natural as the very first sentence to a rushed stranger."
    },
    {
      "id": "good-to-know",
      "title": "Good to know",
      "body": "In Vietnamese, the relationship word is part of the warmth. Getting bạn, anh, chị, or em close enough often matters more than adding extra words."
